From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:27:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] avformat: free buffered packets before the demuxer's private
 data

A demuxer can hand out packets whose buffer is its own memory, with a
free callback that returns the memory to it. The v4l2 input device does
this with its capture buffers: the callback reads the device's private
data to re-queue the buffer with the driver.

avformat_free_context() freed that private data before the packets the
framework still held for the demuxer: the probe packets kept by
avformat_find_stream_info() and the parse and raw queues. A program that
closes an input before reading everything probed, such as ffmpeg when
its output fails to open, therefore ran the v4l2 callback on freed
memory. AddressSanitizer reports it as a heap-use-after-free in the
callback, reached from avpriv_packet_list_free().

Free the buffered packets first. Nothing else in the function uses them,
so freeing them earlier changes nothing for a demuxer whose packets own
their memory.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 libavformat/avformat.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/avformat.c b/libavformat/avformat.c
index 8a98f2e..468240f 100644
--- a/libavformat/avformat.c
+++ b/libavformat/avformat.c
@@ -154,6 +154,14 @@ void avformat_free_context(AVFormatContext *s)
     if (s->oformat && ffofmt(s->oformat)->deinit && fci->initialized)
         ffofmt(s->oformat)->deinit(s);
 
+    /* A packet can reference its demuxer's private data from the free
+     * callback of its buffer, so buffered packets go before that data. */
+    av_packet_free(&si->pkt);
+    av_packet_free(&si->parse_pkt);
+    avpriv_packet_list_free(&si->packet_buffer);
+    if (s->iformat)
+        ff_flush_packet_queue(s);
+
     av_opt_free(s);
     if (s->iformat && s->iformat->priv_class && s->priv_data)
         av_opt_free(s->priv_data);
@@ -183,13 +191,8 @@ void avformat_free_context(AVFormatContext *s)
     av_freep(&s->chapters);
     av_dict_free(&s->metadata);
     av_dict_free(&si->id3v2_meta);
-    av_packet_free(&si->pkt);
-    av_packet_free(&si->parse_pkt);
-    avpriv_packet_list_free(&si->packet_buffer);
     av_freep(&s->streams);
     av_freep(&s->stream_groups);
-    if (s->iformat)
-        ff_flush_packet_queue(s);
     av_freep(&s->url);
     av_freep(&s->name);
     av_free(s);
-- 
